# house-pause-save-commit — open the PAUSE Save submenu (ESC → 3×down → Z), then
# COMMIT a save: press A (Z) on the occupied home slot 0 → the "Overwriting file?
# Are you sure?" choice box → A again confirms Yes → the 60-frame commit animation
# (FUN_004905a8 disk write + the save-progress bar + the selected-card save pulse)
# → back to the resting picker showing the re-saved slot.  Verifies M4c
# (FUN_0047f5bc A-branch + FUN_00434def overwrite dialog + FUN_004905a8 commit).
#
# Derived from house-pause-save-nav (the open path is identical: load fa7c82 →
# HOUSE free-roam idle, {phasepin 80}+{rngseed [80,19937]}; ESC → 3×down → Z opens
# Save; SAVE_PICKER_READY rebases the picker-time inputs past the per-side pause
# open-ramp).  Initial picker state: slot 0 is the only occupied save, so
# last_slot==0 ⇒ cursor=0, scroll=0 — the cursor sits on the OCCUPIED house save.
#
# Commit drive (relative to SAVE_PICKER_READY):
#   A @20 : confirm the home slot.  It is occupied (playtime>0) ⇒ FUN_0047f5bc
#           opens FUN_00434def("Overwriting file?<Are you sure?", 1, 0) with Yes
#           selected, sets DAT_074b28a4=1, plays SE 0x143.
#   A @48 : the box is interactive by now (FUN_00434ed2 ramps af34 1→4 over ~4f);
#           A confirms Yes ⇒ the box close-animates (~7f) then returns 1 ⇒
#           DAT_074b289c (c89c) = 1 → the commit sequence runs (card snapshot +
#           the save jingle + FUN_004905a8(0) working→slot 0 copy/checksum/write)
#           and c89c counts 1→0x3c (60f) driving the progress bar + card pulse.
#   idle  : c89c wraps 0x3c→0, the picker rests showing the re-saved slot 0.
# Presses are 3 frames.  The SAVE virtualization ({savefile}) sandboxes the write
# so the real save is never touched (the harness captures it for verification).
#
# Sync — same TWO rebases as house-pause-save-nav: the option-list nav + Z that
# OPEN the submenu rebase on PAUSE_READY; the commit drive rebases on
# SAVE_PICKER_READY (sub_anim==10 with Save selected — the picker is navigable).
#
# {playtimepin: [0, 29628]} — BILATERAL: force the active slot's total-playtime
# accumulator (the frames@60 the save card shows as TIME) to a canonical origin at
# SAVE_PICKER_READY, AFTER the two completion-based async loads (house + pause menu)
# whose duration is a wall-clock CreateThread race under turbo (port swung ~4000
# frames run-to-run, retail ~40).  Both sides then tick the SAME ~59 input-driven
# frames to the COMMIT snapshot -> occupied_playtime byte-exact.  Placed here (not
# at LOADING_END) because the pause load is the LAST variable load before commit.
# embedded save: fa7c820333914d2a045f1003dc78c4b65fb04235e8d37f032c0f1e0aeb761c54
